From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:30:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Hand the memory cache and PMC
 over with the PMP

ac4e9ecec6 handed the PMP over to Linux, but left out two parts of the
J713 handoff (t8132-j713.dts):

- &mcc with apple,boot-dma-devices = <&pmp>: the PMP keeps doing DMA
  from the boot loader, so the memory cache waits for the PMP driver
  before it allows allocation.
- &pmc with apple,static-voters = <3>: Linux holds the AP's PMC vote
  while the PMP firmware votes as agent 0, and the CLPC child steers the
  GPU power state.

Enable both, as on the J713. Every value matches the J604 ADT (25G83
stub, macOS 26B123):
- MCC apertures at 0x220000000 and 0x222000000, from mcc reg[7] and
  reg[8], with plane-count-per-amcc = 2
- PMC voters and rails inside the pmgr reg[48] window
- voter agents 0:PMP 1:CLPC 2:GFX 3:AP

The T8132 MCC driver does not write if the boot loader has already
enabled the cache, and returns -EBUSY if it finds the cache partly
enabled. With the PMC and CLPC bound, CPU load sets the DCS and fabric
floors, as on the J713.

Fixes: ac4e9ecec6 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Hand the PMP to Linux")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 290674fc37..108f5ea7b6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -711,6 +711,26 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The boot loader leaves the PMP doing DMA through the memory cache, so
+ * cache allocation waits until the PMP driver has bound. The J604 ADT
+ * describes the same two MCC apertures as the J713 (mcc reg[7], reg[8]).
+ */
+&mcc {
+	status = "okay";
+	apple,boot-dma-devices = <&pmp>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * The PMP firmware votes in the PMC as agent 0 from its first steps. The
+ * J604 ADT voter agents are 0:PMP 1:CLPC 2:GFX 3:AP, so agent 3, the AP,
+ * is the static voter, as on the J713.
+ */
+&pmc {
+	status = "okay";
+	apple,static-voters = <3>;
+};
+
 &aop {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-1, DTV-AUD-2, DTV-AUD-13 */
 };
